    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Frequency",
     "texto": [
      "In a simple present-tense sentence, **toujours** (always), **souvent** (often) and **parfois** (sometimes) usually go **after the conjugated verb**, unlike in English («I often go»): **Je vais souvent au cinéma**.",
      "«Never» is **ne … jamais**, which replaces «ne … pas»: **Je ne travaille jamais le dimanche**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Two irregular verbs",
     "texto": [
      "**Aller** (to go) and **faire** (to do) are irregular and very common.",
      "In **Je vais au cinéma**, **à + le** (le cinéma) contracts to **au**. In **à la piscine**, the preposition and the feminine article stay separate.",
      "**Faire du sport** = to do sport."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
